msgid "Quickstart"
msgstr "快速入门"

msgid ""
"The intention of this *quickstart* section is to get you started quickly. "
"Most input is explained using simple examples. Default values are used as "
"much as possible to make the inputs very simple. Naturally, this is by no "
"means an exhaustive description of Molpro. A more systematic and complete "
"explanation of all features of Molpro can be found in the later sections of "
"the manual. We strongly recommend that you read the introductory chapters of"
" the reference manual once you have gained a basic feeling how things are "
"done with Molpro. In particular, the first chapters of the reference manual "
"explain in more detail the use of symmetry, and the data structures (files "
"and records) in Molpro."
msgstr ""
"本\\ *快速入门*\\ 章节旨在帮助您快速上手。大部分输入都通过简单示例进行说明。我们尽可能使用默认值以使输入非常简单。当然，这绝不是对 Molpro"
" 的详尽描述。关于 Molpro 所有功能的更系统、更完整的说明可以在手册的后续章节中找到。我们强烈建议您在对 Molpro "
"的基本操作有初步了解后，阅读参考手册的入门章节。特别是，参考手册的前几章会更详细地解释对称性的使用，以及 Molpro 中的数据结构（文件和记录）。"

msgid ""
"Very simple and mostly self explanatory input for HF, DFT, and most "
"wavefunction correlation methods is described in the following section. "
"Alternatively, a new Molpro user can use the iMolpro graphical user "
"interface, which allows to create inputs for DFT and single-reference "
"methods as well."
msgstr ""
"下一节将描述用于 HF、DFT 和大多数波函数相关方法的非常简单且大多不言自明的输入。或者，新的 Molpro 用户可以使用 iMolpro "
"图形用户界面，它也可以为 DFT 和单参考方法创建输入。"

msgid "Simple input"
msgstr "简单输入"

msgid ""
"it is possible to write Molpro input for DFT and single-reference methods in"
" a single line. A simple DFT geometry calculation can be done as follows:"
msgstr "可以用一行代码编写 Molpro 的 DFT 和单参考方法输入。一个简单的 DFT 几何计算可以按如下方式进行："

msgid "``run DF-KS,b3lyp geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avtz``"
msgstr "``run DF-KS,b3lyp geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avtz``"

msgid ""
"The prefix DF- turns on density fitting approximations for the integrals, "
"which is strongly recommended for efficiency, in particular for larger "
"molecules."
msgstr "前缀 DF- 会为积分开启密度拟合近似，这强烈推荐用于提高效率，特别是对于较大的分子。"

msgid "A most simple example for a CCSD(T) input is:"
msgstr "一个最简单的CCSD(T)输入示例如下："

msgid "``run CCSD(T) geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avtz``"
msgstr "``run CCSD(T) geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avtz``"

msgid "The entries can come in any order, for example"
msgstr "各条目可以按任意顺序排列，例如"

msgid "In detail, the following methods are possible:"
msgstr "具体来说，以下方法是可行的："

msgid ""
"All higher order methods contain the lower-level ones. For example, ccsd(t) "
"contains HF, MP2, and CCSD, and MRCI contains CASPT2."
msgstr "所有高阶方法都包含低阶方法。例如，ccsd(t)包含HF、MP2和CCSD，而MRCI包含CASPT2。"

msgid "The following ones are efficiently implemented:"
msgstr "以下方法已高效实现："

msgid "PNO methods are density fitted in any case."
msgstr "PNO 方法在任何情况下都使用密度拟合。"

msgid ""
"Method, geometry, and basis set are compulsory for running a calculation. By"
" default, only a single energy calculation is done. However, other "
"calculation types can be requested by specifying one of the following "
"directives (the parts in brackets can be omitted or are optional):"
msgstr ""
"方法、几何结构和基组是运行计算所必需的。默认情况下，仅执行单点能计算。但可以通过指定以下指令之一来请求其他计算类型（括号内的部分可以省略或为可选）："

msgid ""
"Note that optg and freq are not possible for PNO methods, since no "
"analytical energy gradients are available."
msgstr "请注意，对于PNO方法，无法使用optg和freq，因为没有可用的解析能量梯度。"

msgid ""
"The following further options are can be given on the run line (alternative "
"values separated by \\|):"
msgstr "以下进一步选项可以在运行行中指定（替代值用\\|分隔）："

msgid ""
"In addition, any valid options for individual methods, as described in the "
"manual, can be given after the command or directives (separated by commas). "
"An example for a DFT frequency calculation with density fitting is"
msgstr "此外，手册中描述的任何适用于单个方法的有效选项，都可以在命令或指令后给出（用逗号分隔）。一个使用密度拟合进行 DFT 频率计算的示例如下："

msgid "Some further examples:"
msgstr "更多示例如下："

msgid "1.) DFT frequency calculation with density fitting:"
msgstr "1.) 使用密度拟合的 DFT 频率计算："

msgid "``run df-ks functional=b3lyp geometry=h2o.xyz basis=def2-tzvp freq``"
msgstr "``run df-ks functional=b3lyp geometry=h2o.xyz basis=def2-tzvp freq``"

msgid "This could also be written as"
msgstr "这也可以写成"

msgid "``run df-ks,b3lyp geometry=h2o.xyz basis=def2-tzvp freq``"
msgstr "``run df-ks,b3lyp geometry=h2o.xyz basis=def2-tzvp freq``"

msgid "The geometry is optimised before computing the hessian."
msgstr "在计算 Hessian 矩阵之前会先优化几何结构。"

msgid ""
"2.) PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 calculation of an intermolecular interaction energy:"
msgstr "2.) 计算分子间相互作用能的 PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 计算："

msgid ""
"``run pno-lccsd(t)-f12,domopt=tight+ geometry=h2odim.xyz basis=avtz,h=vtz "
"interact``"
msgstr ""
"``run pno-lccsd(t)-f12,domopt=tight+ geometry=h2odim.xyz basis=avtz,h=vtz "
"interact``"

msgid "This automatically implies to run a df-hf calculation beforehand."
msgstr "这自动意味着需要先运行一个 df-hf 计算。"

msgid "3.) CCSD(T) with basis set extrapolation:"
msgstr "3.) 使用基组外推的 CCSD(T)："

msgid "``run ccsd(t) geometry=h2o.xyz extrapolate,basis=avtz:avqz``"
msgstr "``run ccsd(t) geometry=h2o.xyz extrapolate,basis=avtz:avqz``"

msgid "This automatically implies HF calculations before the CCSD(T) ones."
msgstr "这自动意味着在 CCSD(T) 计算之前需要进行 HF 计算。"

msgid "4.) Internally contracted MRCI with a CASSCF reference function:"
msgstr "4.) 使用 CASSCF 参考函数的内收缩 MRCI："

msgid "``run mrci geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avqz``"
msgstr "``run mrci geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avqz``"

msgid "5.) Internally contracted CASPT2 with a CASSCF reference function:"
msgstr "5.) 使用 CASSCF 参考函数的内收缩 CASPT2："

msgid "``run caspt2 geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avtz``"
msgstr "``run caspt2 geometry=h2o.xyz basis=avtz``"

msgid "6.) TDDFT excitation energies:"
msgstr "6.) TDDFT 激发能："

msgid ""
"``run df-tddft,states=[4.1,4.2,4.3,4.4] functional=b3lyp basis=avtz "
"geometry=h2o.xyz``"
msgstr ""
"``run df-tddft,states=[4.1,4.2,4.3,4.4] functional=b3lyp basis=avtz "
"geometry=h2o.xyz``"

msgid "This computes 4 excited states for each of the four IRREPS of C2v."
msgstr "这将计算 C2v 点群四个不可约表示中每个的 4 个激发态。"

msgid "7.) CC2 excitation energies:"
msgstr "7.) CC2 激发能："

msgid "``run df-cc2,states=[4.1,4.2,4.3,4.4] basis=avtz geometry=h2o.xyz``"
msgstr "``run df-cc2,states=[4.1,4.2,4.3,4.4] basis=avtz geometry=h2o.xyz``"

msgid ""
"This computes the ground state and 4 excited states for each of the four "
"IRREPS of C2v."
msgstr "这将计算基态以及 C2v 点群四个不可约表示中每个的 4 个激发态。"

msgid ""
"8.)CASSCF calculation using state-averaging over three state symmetries:"
msgstr "8.) 使用三个态对称性进行态平均的 CASSCF 计算："

msgid "``run casscf wfsym=[2,3,1] spin=1 geometry={O;H,O,1.83}``"
msgstr "``run casscf wfsym=[2,3,1] spin=1 geometry={O;H,O,1.83}``"

msgid ""
"This carries out a state-averaged CASSCF calculation for symmetries 2,3,1 "
"(:math:`^2\\Pi_x`,\\ :math:`^2\\Pi_y`, and :math:`^2\\Sigma^+`)."
msgstr ""
"这将对对称性 2,3,1 (:math:`^2\\Pi_x`,\\ :math:`^2\\Pi_y`, 和 :math:`^2\\Sigma^+`) "
"执行态平均 CASSCF 计算。"

msgid ")MRCI calculation using state-averaged CASSCF reference functions:"
msgstr ")使用态平均 CASSCF 参考函数进行 MRCI 计算："

msgid "``run mrci wfsym=[2,3,1] spin=1 geometry={O;H,O,1.83}``"
msgstr "``run mrci wfsym=[2,3,1] spin=1 geometry={O;H,O,1.83}``"

msgid ""
"In this case first a state-averaged CASSCF calculation for symmetries 2,3,1 "
"(:math:`^2\\Pi_x`,\\ :math:`^2\\Pi_y`,  and :math:`^2\\Sigma^+`) is carried "
"out. Subsequently an MRCI calculation is done for each state symmetry "
"separately."
msgstr ""
"在这种情况下，首先对对称性 2,3,1 (:math:`^2\\Pi_x`,\\ :math:`^2\\Pi_y`, 和 "
":math:`^2\\Sigma^+`) 执行态平均 CASSCF 计算。随后，对每个态对称性分别进行 MRCI 计算。"

msgid ""
"10.) Several run command lines can follow each other. For example, compute "
"the lowest ionisation potential of H2O using MRCI:"
msgstr "10.) 多个运行命令行可以依次出现。例如，使用 MRCI 计算 H2O 的最低电离势："

msgid ""
"11.) It is also possible to combine the run command with other standard "
"molpro input, for example:"
msgstr "11.) 也可以将运行命令与其他标准 molpro 输入结合使用，例如："

msgid ""
"The following sections give more basic information about carrying electronic"
" structure calculations with Molpro."
msgstr "以下章节提供了关于使用 Molpro 进行电子结构计算的更多基本信息。"

msgid "How an ab initio calculation works"
msgstr "从头计算如何工作"

msgid ""
"The electronic structure of molecules can be treated only by quantum "
"mechanics, since the electrons are very quickly moving particles. Of course,"
" this manual cannot teach you the underlying theory, and it is assumed that "
"you are familiar with it. We just want to remind you of some basic "
"approximations, which are made in any *ab initio* calculation, independent "
"of which program is used."
msgstr ""
"分子的电子结构只能用量子力学来处理，因为电子是运动非常快的粒子。当然，本手册无法教授您基础理论，并假定您已熟悉它。我们只是想提醒您一些在任何\\ "
"*从头计算*\\ 中都会用到的基本近似，这与使用哪个程序无关。"

msgid ""
"Firstly, the Born-Oppenheimer approximation is applied, which means that the"
" nuclear and electronic motions are decoupled and treated separately (in "
"some cases, non-adiabatic couplings are taken into account at a later "
"stage). Thus, each electronic structure calculation is performed for a fixed"
" nuclear configuration, and therefore the positions of all atoms must be "
"specified in an input file. The *ab initio* program like Molpro then "
"computes the electronic energy by solving the electronic Schrödinger "
"equation for this fixed nuclear configuration. The electronic energy as "
"function of the 3N-6 internal nuclear degrees of freedom defines the "
"potential energy surface (PES). The PES is in general very complicated and "
"can have many minima and saddle points. The minima correspond to equilibrium"
" structures of different isomers or molecules, and saddle points to "
"transition states between them. The aim of most calculations is to find "
"these structures and to characterize the potential and the molecular "
"properties in the vicinity of the stationary points of the PES."
msgstr ""
"首先，应用玻恩-"
"奥本海默近似，这意味着核运动和电子运动被解耦并分开处理（在某些情况下，非绝热耦合会在后续阶段被考虑）。因此，每次电子结构计算都是针对一个固定的核构型进行的，因此所有原子的位置必须在输入文件中指定。像Molpro这样的\\"
" *从头计算*\\ "
"程序随后通过求解该固定核构型下的电子薛定谔方程来计算电子能量。电子能量作为3N-6个内部核自由度的函数定义了势能面（PES）。PES通常非常复杂，可能有许多极小值和鞍点。极小值对应于不同异构体或分子的平衡结构，而鞍点对应于它们之间的过渡态。大多数计算的目标是找到这些结构，并表征PES驻点附近的势能和分子性质。"

msgid ""
"Secondly, the electronic Schrödinger equation cannot be solved exactly, "
"except for very simple systems like the hydrogen atom. Therefore, the "
"electronic wavefunction is represented in certain finite basis sets, and the"
" Schrödinger equation is transformed into an algebraic equation which can be"
" solved using numerical methods. There are two classes of approximations: "
"one concerning the choice of basis functions to represent the one-electron "
"functions called *molecular orbitals*, and one concerning the choice of "
":math:`N`\\ –electron functions to represent the many-electron electronic "
"wavefunction."
msgstr ""
"其次，电子薛定谔方程无法精确求解，除了像氢原子这样的非常简单的系统。因此，电子波函数用某些有限的基组表示，薛定谔方程被转化为一个可以用数值方法求解的代数方程。有两类近似：一类涉及选择基函数来表示称为\\"
" *分子轨道*\\ 的单电子函数，另一类涉及选择 :math:`N`\\ –电子函数来表示多电子电子波函数。"

msgid ""
"In most programs, and also in Molpro, Gaussian basis functions are used to "
"approximate the molecular orbitals, since the required integrals can be "
"computed very quickly in this basis. Many optimized basis sets are available"
" in the Molpro *basis set library*, and in most cases the basis set can be "
"selected using a simple keyword in the input."
msgstr ""
"在大多数程序中，包括Molpro，都使用高斯基函数来近似分子轨道，因为所需的积分可以在这种基组中非常快速地计算。Molpro的\\ *基组库*\\ "
"中提供了许多优化的基组，并且在大多数情况下，可以通过输入中的一个简单关键字来选择基组。"

msgid ""
"The many-electron wavefunction for the molecule is represented as a linear "
"combination of antisymmetrized products (Slater determinants) of the "
"molecular orbitals. In a *full configuration interaction* calculation (FCI) "
"all possible Slater determinants for a given orbital basis are used, and "
"this gives the best possible result for the chosen one-electron basis. "
"However, the number of Slater determinants which can be constructed is "
"enormous, and very quickly increases with the number of electrons and "
"orbitals. Therefore, approximations have to be made, in which the "
"wavefunction is expanded in only a subset of all possible of Slater "
"determinants (or configuration state functions (CSFs), which are symmetry "
"adapted linear combinations of Slater determinants)."
msgstr ""
"分子的多电子波函数表示为分子轨道的反对称化乘积（斯莱特行列式）的线性组合。在\\ *完全组态相互作用*\\ "
"计算（FCI）中，使用给定轨道基组的所有可能的斯莱特行列式，这为所选的一电子基组提供了最佳可能结果。然而，可以构造的斯莱特行列式的数量是巨大的，并且随着电子和轨道数量的增加而迅速增加。因此，必须进行近似，其中波函数仅在所有可能的斯莱特行列式（或组态状态函数（CSFs），它们是斯莱特行列式的对称性适配线性组合）的一个子集中展开。"

msgid ""
"Once such approximations are introduced, it matters how the orbitals are "
"determined. The simplest choice is to use a single Slater determinant and to"
" optimize the orbitals variationally. This is the *Hartree-Fock* (HF) *self "
"consistent field* (SCF) method, and it is usually the first step in any *ab "
"initio* calculation."
msgstr ""
"一旦引入了这样的近似，轨道的确定方式就变得重要。最简单的选择是使用单个斯莱特行列式并变分优化轨道。这就是\\ *Hartree-Fock*\\ "
"（HF）\\ *自洽场*\\ （SCF）方法，它通常是任何\\ *从头计算*\\ 的第一步。"

msgid ""
"In the Hartree-Fock approximation each electron moves in an average "
"potential of the remaining electrons, but has no knowledge of the positions "
"of these. Thus, even though the Coulomb interaction between the electrons is"
" taken into account in an averaged way, the electrons with opposite spin are"
" unable to avoid each other when they come close, and therefore the electron"
" repulsion is overestimated in Hartree-Fock. The purpose of post-Hartree-"
"Fock *electron correlation* methods is to correct for this by taking the "
"instantaneous correlation of the electrons into account. The corresponding "
"energy lowering is called *electron correlation energy*. There are many "
"different methods available and implemented in Molpro to approximate and "
"optimize the wavefunction, for instance Møller-Plesset (MP) perturbation "
"theory, configuration interaction (CI), or coupled cluster (CC) methods. "
"Also density functional (DFT) methods take into account electron "
"correlation, even though in a less systematic and less well defined way than"
" *ab initio* methods."
msgstr ""
"在Hartree-"
"Fock近似中，每个电子在其余电子的平均势中运动，但不知道这些电子的位置。因此，尽管电子之间的库仑相互作用以平均方式被考虑，但自旋相反的电子在靠近时无法相互避开，因此电子排斥在Hartree-"
"Fock中被高估了。后Hartree-Fock\\ *电子相关*\\ 方法的目的是通过考虑电子的瞬时相关性来纠正这一点。相应的能量降低称为\\ "
"*电子相关能*\\ 。有许多不同的方法可用并在Molpro中实现，以近似和优化波函数，例如Møller-"
"Plesset（MP）微扰理论、组态相互作用（CI）或耦合簇（CC）方法。密度泛函（DFT）方法也考虑了电子相关，尽管其方式不如\\ *从头计算*\\ "
"方法系统和完善。"

msgid ""
"One point of warning should be noticed here: electron correlation treatments"
" require much larger one-electron basis sets than Hartree-Fock or DFT to "
"yield converged results. Such calculations can therefore be expensive. For a"
" fixed basis set, a correlation calculation is usually much more expensive "
"than a HF calculation, and therefore many unexperienced people are tempted "
"to use small basis sets for a correlation calculation. However, this is not "
"reasonable at all, and for meaningful calculations one should at least use a"
" triple-zeta basis with several polarization functions (e.g. cc-pVTZ). Using"
" explicitly-correlated methods discussed later, the basis set problem is "
"much alleviated."
msgstr ""
"这里需要注意一点警告：电子相关处理需要比 Hartree-Fock 或 DFT "
"大得多的单电子基组才能获得收敛的结果。因此，这类计算可能非常昂贵。对于固定的基组，相关计算通常比 HF "
"计算昂贵得多，因此许多经验不足的人倾向于在相关计算中使用小基组。然而，这完全不合理，对于有意义的计算，至少应使用带有多个极化函数的三ζ基组（例如 cc-"
"pVTZ）。使用后面讨论的显式相关方法，基组问题会大大缓解。"

msgid ""
"Finally, it should also be noted that the HF approximation, and all single "
"reference methods which use the HF determinant as zeroth order "
"approximation, are usually only appropriate near the equilibrium structures."
" In most cases they are not able to dissociate molecular bonds correctly, or"
" to describe electronically excited or (nearly) degenerate states. In such "
"cases multireference methods, which use a multiconfiguration SCF "
"wavefunctions (MCSCF) as zeroth order approximation, offer a reasonable "
"alternative. Complete active space SCF (CASSCF) is a special variant of "
"MCSCF. In Molpro various multireference electron correlation methods are "
"implemented, e.g., multireference perturbation theory (MRPT, CASPT2) and "
"multireference configuration interaction (MRCI), and variants of these such "
"as multireference coupled-pair functional (MR-ACPF)."
msgstr ""
"最后，还应注意，HF 近似以及所有使用 HF "
"行列式作为零级近似的单参考方法，通常仅适用于平衡结构附近。在大多数情况下，它们无法正确解离分子键，或描述电子激发态或（近）简并态。在这种情况下，使用多组态"
" SCF 波函数（MCSCF）作为零级近似的多参考方法提供了一个合理的替代方案。完全活性空间 SCF（CASSCF）是 MCSCF 的一种特殊变体。在 "
"Molpro 中实现了各种多参考电子相关方法，例如，多参考微扰理论（MRPT, "
"CASPT2）和多参考组态相互作用（MRCI），以及这些方法的变体，如多参考耦合对泛函（MR-ACPF）。"

msgid ""
"As you will see, it is quite easy to run an electronic structure calculation"
" using Molpro, and probably you will have done your first successful run "
"within the next 10 minutes. However, the art is to know which basis set and "
"method to use for a particular problem in order to obtain an accurate result"
" for a minimum possible cost. This is something which needs a lot of "
"experience and which we cannot teach you here. We can only encourage you not"
" to use Molpro or any other popular electronic structure program simply as a"
" black box without any understanding or critical assessment of the methods "
"and results!"
msgstr ""
"正如你将看到的，使用 Molpro 运行电子结构计算非常容易，很可能在接下来的 10 "
"分钟内你就会完成第一次成功的运行。然而，关键在于知道针对特定问题使用哪种基组和方法，以便以尽可能低的成本获得准确的结果。这需要大量的经验，我们无法在此教授。我们只能鼓励你不要将"
" Molpro 或任何其他流行的电子结构程序简单地当作黑箱使用，而不对方法和结果有任何理解或批判性评估！"

msgid ""
"Literature: `//Introduction to Computational Chemistry//, F. Jensen, Wiley, "
"2006 <http://www.amazon.com/Introduction-Computational-Chemistry-Frank-"
"Jensen/dp/0470011874/ref=ed_oe_p>`__"
msgstr ""
"文献：\\ `//Introduction to Computational Chemistry//, F. Jensen, Wiley, 2006 "
"<http://www.amazon.com/Introduction-Computational-Chemistry-Frank-"
"Jensen/dp/0470011874/ref=ed_oe_p>`__"

msgid "How to run Molpro"
msgstr "如何运行 Molpro"

msgid ""
"Simple examples for input files will be given in the following sections. "
"Once the input file is ready, a Molpro calculation can be started using the "
"``molpro`` command. Assume the input file is called ``h2o.inp``. The command"
" to run Molpro is then simply"
msgstr ""
"输入文件的简单示例将在以下章节中给出。一旦输入文件准备就绪，就可以使用 ``molpro`` 命令启动 Molpro 计算。假设输入文件名为 "
"``h2o.inp``\\ 。那么运行 Molpro 的命令很简单"

msgid ""
"would not save an existing output file but simply overwrite it. If you want "
"to give your output a different name than the default one, you can use the "
"``-o`` option, for instance"
msgstr "将不会保存现有的输出文件，而是直接覆盖它。如果您希望为输出指定一个不同于默认值的名称，可以使用 ``-o`` 选项，例如"

msgid ""
"There are many other options for the ``molpro`` command, most of which, "
"however, do not often need to be specified. You can find a full description "
"in the Molpro reference manual. Some of the more important ones are"
msgstr ""
"``molpro`` 命令还有许多其他选项，但其中大多数通常不需要指定。您可以在 Molpro 参考手册中找到完整的描述。一些较为重要的选项包括"

msgid ""
"The amount of memory Molpro is allowed to use can be specified using the "
"``-m`` option, e.g., ``molpro -m 4M h2o.inp`` & This means that 4 megawords "
"(MW) of memory are allocated by molpro (see also ``memory`` input card, "
"section `memory control <quickstart.html#memory-control>`__."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 ``-m`` 选项指定 Molpro 允许使用的内存量，例如，\\ ``molpro -m 4M h2o.inp`` & 这意味着 "
"molpro 分配了 4 兆字（MW）的内存（另请参见 ``memory`` 输入卡，章节 `memory control "
"<quickstart.html#memory-control>`__\\ 。"

msgid ""
"For running in parallel (assuming that the program has been suitably "
"compiled), ``molpro -n 8 h2o.inp`` & will run 8 cooperative processes. "
"Depending on how the program has been built, this will result in 7- or 8-way"
" parallel execution."
msgstr ""
"对于并行运行（假设程序已适当编译），\\ ``molpro -n 8 h2o.inp`` & 将运行 8 个协作进程。根据程序的构建方式，这将导致 7 "
"路或 8 路并行执行。"

msgid ""
"Optionally, but not by default, it is possible so specify one or more named "
"files in the input, and these are used by the program to store intermediate "
"parameters and results, that can be used to restart (see section `restarting"
" calculations <quickstart.html#restarting-calculations>`__). If nothing is "
"given in the input, these files are still present, but they are temporary, "
"and disappear at the end of the job. For performance reasons, the program "
"runs in scratch directory, for example a high-performance file system. By "
"default, the location of this directory is ``/tmp/$USER``, or taken from the"
" environment variable TMPDIR (if set), but it can be controlled using the "
"``-d`` option, for example ``molpro -d /scratch/$USER h2o.inp`` & At the end"
" of the job, the named files are copied to a permanent location. The most "
"important file for a restart is file 2, which contains the wave function "
"information (cf. section `restarting calculations "
"<quickstart.html#restarting-calculations>`__). By default, this file is "
"copied into the directory $HOME/wfu, but this directory can be changed with "
"the -W option. At the beginning of the job, if appropriate files exist in "
"the permanent location, they are copied in to the scratch directory."
msgstr ""
"可选地（但默认不启用），可以在输入中指定一个或多个命名文件，程序使用这些文件来存储中间参数和结果，这些文件可用于重启计算（参见 `restarting "
"calculations <quickstart.html#restarting-calculations>`__ "
"节）。如果输入中未指定任何文件，这些文件仍然存在，但它们是临时的，并在作业结束时消失。出于性能考虑，程序在临时目录（例如高性能文件系统）中运行。默认情况下，该目录的位置是"
" ``/tmp/$USER``\\ ，或取自环境变量 TMPDIR（如果已设置），但可以使用 ``-d`` 选项控制，例如 ``molpro -d "
"/scratch/$USER h2o.inp`` & 作业结束时，命名文件会被复制到永久位置。用于重启的最重要文件是文件 2，它包含波函数信息（参见 "
"`restarting calculations <quickstart.html#restarting-calculations>`__ "
"节）。默认情况下，此文件被复制到目录 $HOME/wfu 中，但该目录可以通过 -W "
"选项更改。作业开始时，如果永久位置存在合适的文件，它们会被复制到临时目录中。"

msgid "How to prepare an input file"
msgstr "如何准备输入文件"

msgid ""
"As explained in the introduction, the input file should contain the "
"following minimum information."
msgstr "如引言所述，输入文件应包含以下最低限度的信息。"

msgid "Geometry specification."
msgstr "几何结构指定。"

msgid "Specification of one-electron basis set (although there is a default)."
msgstr "单电子基组指定（尽管有默认值）。"

msgid ""
"Specification of the method to compute the many-electron wavefunction. "
"Several calculations of different type can follow each other."
msgstr "计算多电子波函数的方法指定。可以连续进行多个不同类型的计算。"

msgid "We will consider these three in turn."
msgstr "我们将依次考虑这三项。"

msgid ""
"All input can be given in upper or lower case and in free format. Most input"
" lines start with a keyword, which is followed by numbers or other "
"specifications (options). The different entries on each line should be "
"separated by commas (see next section for more explanation about this)."
msgstr ""
"所有输入可以大写或小写，并采用自由格式。大多数输入行以关键字开头，后跟数字或其他规范（选项）。每行上的不同条目应以逗号分隔（有关此点的更多说明，请参见下一节）。"

msgid "Geometry specification"
msgstr "几何结构指定"

msgid ""
"The simplest way to specify the coordinates of the atoms is to use cartesian"
" coordinates and the *XYZ* input format, which is standard in many programs."
" In this case the geometry input looks as follows (example for "
"formaldehyde)."
msgstr ""
"指定原子坐标最简单的方法是使用笛卡尔坐标和\\ *XYZ*\\ 输入格式，这在许多程序中是标准做法。在这种情况下，几何结构输入如下所示（以甲醛为例）。"

msgid ""
"Alternatively, the geometry can be specified in the *Z–matrix* form, which "
"is also used in many other programs. In this case, the geometry is defined "
"by distances and angles. This is a little more involved, and here we give "
"only a simple example, again for formaldehyde."
msgstr ""
"或者，也可以使用\\ *Z–矩阵*\\ "
"形式来指定几何结构，这种形式也在许多其他程序中使用。在这种情况下，几何结构通过距离和角度来定义。这稍微复杂一些，这里我们仅给出一个简单的例子，同样以甲醛为例。"

msgid ""
"Here, 1.182 and 1.102 are the C-O and the C-H bond distances, respectively. "
"122.1789 is the H-O-C angle, and 180 is the angle between the H1-C-O and "
"H2-C-O planes (dihedral angle). Note that by default the bond distances are "
"in atomic units (bohr), but one can give the ``angstrom`` keyword to use "
"Ångstrøm."
msgstr ""
"此处，1.182 和 1.102 分别是 C-O 和 C-H 的键长。122.1789 是 H-O-C 角，而 180 是 H1-C-O 和 "
"H2-C-O 平面之间的夹角（二面角）。请注意，默认情况下键长以原子单位（波尔）给出，但可以通过指定 ``angstrom`` 关键字来使用 "
"Ångstrøm。"

msgid ""
"As an alternative to the *xyz* input explained above, it is also possible to"
" specify cartesian coordinates in a Z–matrix. In this case the form is"
msgstr "作为上述 *xyz* 输入的替代方案，也可以在 Z–矩阵中指定笛卡尔坐标。此时，其形式为"

msgid ""
"Instead of constant numbers it is also possible to use variables in the "
"Z–matrix input. For instance, the input for formaldehyde can be written as"
msgstr "在 Z–矩阵输入中，除了使用常数外，也可以使用变量。例如，甲醛的输入可以写为"

msgid ""
"The values of the variables can be changed in the course of the "
"calculations, so that calculations can be performed for different geometries"
" in one run. This will be explained in more detail later."
msgstr "变量的值可以在计算过程中改变，从而可以在一次运行中为不同的几何结构进行计算。这将在后面更详细地解释。"

msgid ""
"By default, the program repositions and rotates the molecule so that the "
"coordinate axes have the centre of mass of the molecule as origin, and are "
"aligned with the principal inertial axes. This behaviour is usually what is "
"required, in order that the program can recognize and exploit point-group "
"symmetry, but can be changed through parameters specified on the ``ORIENT`` "
"command (see manual). By default, the program tries to find and use the "
"maximum abelian point-group symmetry, but this behaviour can be controlled "
"using the ``SYMMETRY`` command (see manual)."
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，程序会重新定位和旋转分子，使得坐标轴以分子的质心为原点，并与主惯性轴对齐。这种行为通常是必需的，以便程序能够识别并利用点群对称性，但可以通过在"
" ``ORIENT`` 命令上指定的参数来更改（参见手册）。默认情况下，程序尝试寻找并使用最大的阿贝尔点群对称性，但可以使用 ``SYMMETRY`` "
"命令来控制此行为（参见手册）。"

msgid "Basis set specification"
msgstr "基组指定"

msgid ""
"In many cases the one-electron basis set can be specified in the simple form"
msgstr "在许多情况下，单电子基组可以用简单的形式指定"

msgid ""
"where *name* refers to the basis set name in the library. You can find all "
"possible basis sets on the Molpro Web page. Popular and often used for high-"
"level calculations are the correlation-consistent polarized basis sets of "
"Dunning and coworkers, denoted ``cc-pVDZ`` (double zeta), ``cc-pVTZ`` "
"(triple zeta), ``cc-pVQZ`` (quadruple zeta), ``cc-pV5Z`` (quintuple zeta). "
"These names can be used directly or abbreviated by ``VDZ``, ``VTZ``, ``VQZ``"
" and so on. For computing certain properties like electron affinities, "
"polarizabilities, or intermolecular potentials additional diffuse basis "
"functions are needed, and such functions are included in the augmented "
"correlation-consistent basis sets, denoted ``aug-cc-pVDZ``, ``aug-cc-pVTZ`` "
"etc. These names can be abbreviated by ``AVDZ``, ``AVTZ``, ``AVQZ`` etc."
msgstr ""
"其中 *名称* 指的是库中的基组名称。您可以在 Molpro 网页上找到所有可能的基组。常用于高水平计算的是 Dunning "
"及其同事的相关一致极化基组，表示为 ``cc-pVDZ``\\ （双 zeta）、\\ ``cc-pVTZ``\\ （三 zeta）、\\ ``cc-"
"pVQZ``\\ （四 zeta）、\\ ``cc-pV5Z``\\ （五 zeta）。这些名称可以直接使用或缩写为 ``VDZ``\\ 、\\ "
"``VTZ``\\ 、\\ ``VQZ`` "
"等。为了计算某些性质，如电子亲和能、极化率或分子间势能，需要额外的弥散基函数，这些函数包含在增强的相关一致基组中，表示为 ``aug-cc-"
"pVDZ``\\ 、\\ ``aug-cc-pVTZ`` 等。这些名称可以缩写为 ``AVDZ``\\ 、\\ ``AVTZ``\\ 、\\ "
"``AVQZ`` 等。"

msgid ""
"Another popular choice are the Gaussian basis sets of Pople and coworkers, "
"e.g. ``6-31G**`` (double zeta), ``6-311G(2DF,2PD)`` (triple zeta), "
"``6-311G++(2DF,2PD)`` (augmented triple zeta) etc. It should be noted here "
"that by default Molpro uses spherical harmonics (:math:`5d`, :math:`7f` "
"etc), while ``Gaussian`` uses cartesian functions (:math:`6d`, :math:`10f` "
"etc). This yields slightly different energies. Cartesian functions can also "
"be used in Molpro, but then the keyword"
msgstr ""
"另一个流行的选择是 Pople 及其同事的高斯基组，例如 ``6-31G**``\\ （双 zeta）、\\ ``6-311G(2DF,2PD)``\\"
" （三 zeta）、\\ ``6-311G++(2DF,2PD)``\\ （增强三 zeta）等。这里需要注意的是，默认情况下 Molpro "
"使用球谐函数（\\ :math:`5d`\\ 、\\ :math:`7f` 等），而 ``Gaussian`` 使用笛卡尔函数（\\ "
":math:`6d`\\ 、\\ :math:`10f` 等）。这会产生略微不同的能量。Molpro 中也可以使用笛卡尔函数，但需要指定关键字"

msgid "``cartesian``"
msgstr "``cartesian``"

msgid "has to be given before the basis set specification."
msgstr "必须在基组指定之前给出。"

msgid ""
"It also possible to use different basis sets for different atoms. In this "
"case the simplest input reads for example"
msgstr "也可以为不同的原子使用不同的基组。在这种情况下，最简单的输入示例如下"

msgid "``basis,c=vtz,o=avtz,h=vdz``"
msgstr "``basis,c=vtz,o=avtz,h=vdz``"

msgid ""
"Basis sets can also be specified manually (exponents and contraction "
"coefficients). Refer to the Molpro reference manual for details."
msgstr "基组也可以手动指定（指数和收缩系数）。详情请参阅 Molpro 参考手册。"

msgid ""
"If no basis set is specified at all, Molpro uses ``cc-pVDZ``, but this does "
"not mean that this is a sensible choice!"
msgstr "如果完全没有指定基组，Molpro 会使用 ``cc-pVDZ``\\ ，但这并不意味着这是一个明智的选择！"

msgid "Method and wavefunction specification"
msgstr "方法和波函数指定"

msgid "Variables"
msgstr "变量"

msgid ""
"Molpro stores all important results in variables. For example, the Hartree-"
"Fock program sets the variables ``ENERGY, DMX, DMY, DMZ``, holding the final"
" energy and dipole moments. These variables can be used for further "
"analysis. For a list of variables set by other programs see section "
"`variables <quickstart.html#variables>`__. Variables can be used in "
"expressions, quite similar to fortran."
msgstr ""
"Molpro将所有重要结果存储在变量中。例如，Hartree-Fock程序会设置变量\\ ``ENERGY, DMX, DMY, DMZ``\\ "
"，用于保存最终能量和偶极矩。这些变量可用于进一步分析。有关其他程序设置的变量列表，请参阅\\ `variables "
"<quickstart.html#variables>`__\\ 节。变量可在表达式中使用，与Fortran非常相似。"

msgid ""
"For example, it is possible to compute a reaction energy in one job. Let’s "
"take CO + H\\ :math:`_2` :math:`\\rightarrow` H\\ :math:`_2`\\ CO as a "
"simple example."
msgstr ""
"例如，可以在一个作业中计算反应能。我们以CO + H\\ :math:`_2` :math:`\\rightarrow` H\\ "
":math:`_2`\\ CO作为一个简单示例。"

msgid "Hartree-Fock"
msgstr "Hartree-Fock"

msgid "Closed-shell Hartree-Fock calculations"
msgstr "闭壳层Hartree-Fock计算"

msgid "The Hartree-Fock program is invoked by the command"
msgstr "Hartree-Fock程序通过以下命令调用"

msgid "``hf``"
msgstr "``hf``"

msgid ""
"The program will then first compute the one-and two-electron integrals and "
"store these on disk. Once this step is completed, the self-consistent field "
"calculation, which is iterative, is carried out, using the precomputed "
"integrals (for integral-direct calculations, in which the integrals are not "
"stored but recomputed whenever needed, see section `Integral-direct "
"calculations <quickstart.html#integral-direct-calculations>`__)."
msgstr ""
"程序将首先计算单电子和双电子积分并将其存储在磁盘上。此步骤完成后，将使用预先计算的积分进行自洽场计算（该计算是迭代的）（有关积分直接计算，即积分不存储而是在需要时重新计算，请参阅\\"
" `Integral-direct calculations <quickstart.html#integral-direct-"
"calculations>`__\\ 节）。"

msgid ""
"Now you are ready to try your first Molpro calculation. The complete input "
"for a HF calculation for formaldehyde is"
msgstr "现在，您可以尝试进行第一次Molpro计算。甲醛HF计算的完整输入如下："

msgid ""
"The first line, starting with ``**`` is optional and is used to specify a "
"title. The last line, ``—`` is also optional. This indicates the end of the "
"input; any further input after ``—`` is ignored. Any text written after an "
"exclamation mark is treated as comment and also ignored. Blanks and blank "
"lines have no effect."
msgstr ""
"第一行以\\ ``**``\\ 开头，是可选的，用于指定标题。最后一行\\ ``—``\\ 也是可选的。它表示输入结束；\\ ``—``\\ "
"之后的任何进一步输入都将被忽略。感叹号后书写的任何文本均被视为注释，同样会被忽略。空格和空行没有影响。"

msgid ""
"If you inspect the output, you will find that Molpro detected that the "
"molecule has :math:`C_{2v}` symmetry, and that there are 5 orbitals "
"belonging to the irreducible representation :math:`a_1`, one belonging to "
":math:`b_1`, and two to :math:`b_2`. In Molpro the irreducible "
"representations are numbered, and in the :math:`C_{2v}` group the numbering "
"is 1–4 for :math:`a_1`, :math:`b_1`, :math:`b_2`, and :math:`a_2`, "
"respectively. The third orbital in symmetry :math:`a_1` is denoted 3.1, the "
"second orbital in symmetry :math:`b_2` is denoted 2.3. Please take a little "
"time to study the output in order to understand these conventions."
msgstr ""
"如果您检查输出，会发现Molpro检测到该分子具有\\ :math:`C_{2v}`\\ 对称性，并且有5个轨道属于不可约表示\\ "
":math:`a_1`\\ ，1个属于\\ :math:`b_1`\\ ，2个属于\\ :math:`b_2`\\ "
"。在Molpro中，不可约表示被编号，在\\ :math:`C_{2v}`\\ 群中，编号1–4分别对应\\ :math:`a_1`\\ 、\\ "
":math:`b_1`\\ 、\\ :math:`b_2`\\ 和\\ :math:`a_2`\\ 。对称性\\ :math:`a_1`\\ "
"中的第三个轨道记为3.1，对称性\\ :math:`b_2`\\ 中的第二个轨道记为2.3。请花一点时间研究输出，以理解这些约定。"

msgid ""
"In the current case, Molpro has worked out the number of occupied orbitals "
"in each symmetry automatically according to the Aufbau principle. This works"
" in most but not all cases. You can specify the number of occupied orbitals "
"in each symmetry using the ``occ`` directive. In the current case, it would "
"read"
msgstr ""
"在当前情况下，Molpro已根据奥夫鲍原理自动计算出了每个对称性中的占据轨道数。这在大多数情况下有效，但并非总是如此。您可以使用\\ ``occ``\\"
" 指令指定每个对称性中的占据轨道数。在当前情况下，它将写作"

msgid "``occ,5,1,2``"
msgstr "``occ,5,1,2``"

msgid "and the meaning of this should be quite obvious from the above."
msgstr "其含义从上述内容来看应该相当明显。"

msgid ""
"If special directives are given for a command, like above ``occ`` is a "
"directive for command ``hf``, the command and the associated directives have"
" to be enclosed by curly brackets, e.g."
msgstr "如果为某个命令给出了特殊指令，例如上面的\\ ``occ``\\ 是命令\\ ``hf``\\ 的指令，则该命令及其关联指令必须用花括号括起来，例如"

msgid ""
"This is called a command block. The curly brackets are needed to avoid "
"ambiguities, since some directives can also be used outside command blocks. "
"Please refer to the manual for more details."
msgstr "这称为命令块。花括号是必需的，以避免歧义，因为某些指令也可以在命令块之外使用。更多详情请参阅手册。"

msgid ""
"Each command or directive can either begin on a new line, or be separated by"
" semicolons. For instance"
msgstr "每个命令或指令可以另起一行开始，也可以用分号分隔。例如"

msgid "is equivalent to the previous example."
msgstr "与前面的例子是等价的。"

msgid "Open-shell Hartree-Fock calculations"
msgstr "开壳层 Hartree-Fock 计算"

msgid ""
"In the above example all orbitals are doubly occupied, and therefore the "
"total symmetry of the ground state wavefunction, which is the direct product"
" of the spin-orbital symmetries, is :math:`A_1`. Since all electrons are "
"paired, it is a singlet wavefunction, :math:`^1A_1`."
msgstr ""
"在上面的例子中，所有轨道都是双占据的，因此基态波函数的总对称性（即自旋轨道对称性的直积）为 :math:`A_1`\\ "
"。由于所有电子都已配对，它是一个单重态波函数 :math:`^1A_1`\\ 。"

msgid ""
"Even though most stable molecules in the electronic ground states are "
"closed-shell singlet states, this is not always the case. Open-shell "
"treatments are necessary for radicals or ions. As a first simple example we "
"consider the positive ion of formaldehyde, H\\ :math:`_2`\\ CO\\ :math:`^+`."
" In this case it turns out that the lowest cation state is :math:`^2B_2`, "
"i.e., one electron is removed from the highest occupied orbital in symmetry "
":math:`b_2` (denoted 2.3 in Molpro, see above). By default Molpro assumes "
"that the number of electrons equals the total nuclear charge. Therefore, in "
"order to compute an ion, one has to specify the number of electrons. "
"Alternatively, the total charge of the molecule can be given (see below). "
"Furthermore, one has to specify the symmetry and spin of the wavefunction. "
"This is done using the ``wf`` directive (``wf`` stands for *wavefunction*):"
msgstr ""
"尽管大多数稳定分子在电子基态时是闭壳层单重态，但情况并非总是如此。对于自由基或离子，需要进行开壳层处理。作为第一个简单的例子，我们考虑甲醛的正离子 "
"H\\ :math:`_2`\\ CO\\ :math:`^+`\\ 。在这种情况下，最低的阳离子态是 :math:`^2B_2`\\ ，即从对称性为 "
":math:`b_2` 的最高占据轨道（在 Molpro 中记为 2.3，见上文）中移除了一个电子。默认情况下，Molpro "
"假设电子数等于总核电荷。因此，为了计算离子，必须指定电子数。或者，可以给出分子的总电荷（见下文）。此外，还必须指定波函数的对称性和自旋。这是通过 "
"``wf`` 指令（\\ ``wf`` 代表 *wavefunction*\\ ）完成的："

msgid "``wf,15,3,1``"
msgstr "``wf,15,3,1``"

msgid ""
"The first entry on a ``wf`` card is the number of electrons. The second "
"entry is the total symmetry of the wavefunction. For a doublet this equals "
"the symmetry of the singly occupied molecular orbital. Finally, the third "
"entry specifies the number of singly occupied orbitals, or, more generally "
"the total spin. Zero means singlet, 1 doublet, 2 triplet and so on. "
"Alternatively, the ``WF`` card can be written in the form"
msgstr ""
"``wf`` "
"卡片上的第一个条目是电子数。第二个条目是波函数的总对称性。对于双重态，这等于单占据分子轨道的对称性。最后，第三个条目指定单占据轨道的数量，或者更一般地说，指定总自旋。0"
